      "id": 145904,
      "name": "MigrantP",
      "username": "MigrantP",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/migrantp/{size}/1921_2.png",
      "created_at": "2015-08-10T16:26:00.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Pydro\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/pydro/48/1844_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Pydro:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>What's interesting though is that Summon Staff was changed so that <a href=\"https://trello.com/c/xXxG4IDt/27-if-summon-staff-does-not-find-a-staff-of-ra-the-deck-is-not-shuffled\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">if there are no Staves in the deck, the deck isn't shuffled.</a></p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>\"If there are no Staves in the deck, the deck isn't shuffled\" was the bug that was fixed in version 1.4.1. Now, the deck is always shuffled.</p>\n<p>We discussed with Christopher, and \"shuffle the trash into the deck\" should cause a shuffle even when the trash is empty. This will be fixed in an update.</p>\n<p>Note: on the tabletop, if you don't know anything about the state of the deck, it makes no difference whether you shuffle in that case from an information POV.</p>",
      "post_number": 13,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:23:44.721Z",
